{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:4591-1","published":"2026-10-08T12:18:31Z","modified":"2026-10-09T18:15:03.742602908Z","related":["CVE-2026-18374","CVE-2026-19542","CVE-2026-6368","CVE-2026-6791","CVE-2026-77117","CVE-2026-80489","CVE-2026-8674","CVE-2026-86805","CVE-2026-89092","CVE-2026-97399"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-18374","CVE-2026-19542","CVE-2026-6368","CVE-2026-6791","CVE-2026-77117","CVE-2026-80489","CVE-2026-8674","CVE-2026-86805","CVE-2026-89092","CVE-2026-97399"],"summary":"Security update for glibc","details":"This update for glibc fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-6368: wordexp WRDE_APPEND rollback restores stale we_wordv, leading to invalid free in wordfree\n  (bsc#1274726).\n- CVE-2026-6791: wordexp: unbounded alloca (strndupa) in parse_tilde (bsc#1274723).\n- CVE-2026-8674: reachable assert in `resolv/resolv_conf.c:update_from_conf` allows an attacker in a local network to\n  trigger a process crash (bsc#1281297).\n- CVE-2026-18374: overflow in the fopen ccs extension (bsc#1277262).\n- CVE-2026-19542: Fix out-of-bounds array write in tdelete (bsc#1276946).\n- CVE-2026-77117: non-progress DoS in SHIFT_JISX0213 -&gt; UCS-4 conversion state handling (bsc#1277921).\n- CVE-2026-80489: non-progress DoS in SHIFT_JISX0213 -&gt; UCS-4 conversion state handling (bsc#1277922).\n- CVE-2026-86805: TOCTOU race condition in the dynamic loader allows local attackers to escalate privileges\n  (bsc#1282509).\n- CVE-2026-89092: nscd stack overflow leads to degraded DNS resolution (bsc#1282449).\n- CVE-2026-97399: one byte out-of-bounds read via function `strncasecmp` on Power8 can lead to a program crash\n  (bsc#1283147).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"glibc","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Micro 5.3","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/glibc&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Micro%205.3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.31-150300.109.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"glibc":"2.31-150300.109.1","glibc-devel":